When max_norm is not None, Embeddings forward method will modify the weight tensor in-place. Since tensors needed for gradient computations cannot be modified in-place, performing a differentiable operation on Embedding.weight before calling Embeddings forward method requires cloning Embedding.weight when max_norm is not None. For example:
None
Embedding
Embedding.weight
n, d, m = 3, 5, 7 embedding = nn.Embedding(n, d, max_norm=1.0) W = torch.randn((m, d), requires_grad=True) idx = torch.tensor([1, 2]) a = embedding.weight.clone() @ W.t() # weight must be cloned for this to be differentiable b = embedding(idx) @ W.t() # modifies weight in-place out = (a.unsqueeze(0) + b.unsqueeze(1)) loss = out.sigmoid().prod() loss.backward()
